what the container actually recomputed, of the numbers the text cites
==========================================================================
  A  distinct values in the body            : 191
  B  of those, reconciled by step127        : 173
  C  of B, source table regenerated here    : 131
     audited but NOT regenerated            : 42
     source not established either way      : 1

  S54 section 8 threshold is C / A >= 50%: 131 / 191 = 68.6%
  with the 1 unestablished values counted the other way,
  the figure is 132 / 191 = 69.1%. The threshold is MET either
  way only if those two agree -- here they do.

  NOTE Being audited is not being recomputed. step127 checks a number
  against a table; that table may have been mounted in from the
  authoring machine. The tables behind the coloc, SMR, meta,
  single-cell and chromatin numbers are not regenerated in the
  container because their inputs are not distributed.

